wildlife.prompt:
Use case: precise-object-edit. Correct the LAYOUT ONLY of this wildlife sprite atlas while preserving all ten charming illustrated subjects and their style.
The required layout is an EXACT invisible grid of 2 equal columns and 5 equal rows on a 2:3 portrait transparent PNG. Each object must be wholly inside its cell with generous genuinely alpha-transparent gutter on all four sides. Shrink each subject by roughly 25% from its present size and place its center at the geometric center of its cell. No object may cross a row or column boundary.
For a 1024x1536 canvas use cell centers: x=256 and768; row centers y=154,461,768,1075,1382. Keep every object's visible pixels at least24px from top/bottom cell boundaries and50px from left/right boundaries. Exact order:
row1 deer waving / rabbit waving;
row2 raccoon waving / bear waving;
row3 one blue bird flying / one brown bird flying;
row4 squirrel waving / turtle;
row5 orange leaf / yellow butterfly.
Maintain complete silhouettes, fur/feathers, antlers, feet, tails and wings without clipping. Keep warm expressive faces and waving poses. Keep single animals or items with no added elements.
Output must have real, clean alpha transparency outside every subject, no colored haze, white/gray matte or edge fringe, painted background, shadows, ground, floor, grid, labels or extra speckles. Do not draw a checkerboard. Only the ten isolated objects in the exact grid.
